 @thejollysloth5743  Nvidia works with more developers to make sure their products work well out of the box. AMD seems to do this less. This is a reason AMD catches up later after it has been optimized better. 
Nvidia 10 series had excellent rasterization optimization for Directx 11 but Directx12 games had a bit of a performance hit... initially. It seems it has gotten better. They are pretty comparable now with some titles running better on AMD and some on Nvidia.
I feel at the moment the 6 Series raytracing performance on their lower end cards is not a good as Nvidia's current lower end cards. 3060-3070ti.

 @JohnCiaccio  I'm sticking with 1080p high refresh rate for another few years, until 1440p monitors and GPU's are the new £200 monitors and £350 GPU's.
It will happen eventually, but I'm not spending an extra £700+ to play at 1440p 144hz.
I also think AMD FSR will get better and be implimented in more games.  We'll just have to see what happens.  This is my first AMD card, but when the 3060 is worse than the 6600 xt and costs way more in my area I'm just hapy to have upgraded from the 1060 for £100 and getting over double the performance.

